{"summary":"Reject the compile-failure amendment and the molt-stress snapshot amendment because the current tree already compiles and already reports molt-stress suppression correctly. Accept the remaining amendments: egg_drop_temp_swing_c is a dead runtime knob, HighDensity is unused event surface, sudden egg-drop behavior is regressed by smoothing-only gating, and reproduction_factors currently has two deterministic failures.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-5-1cf2cbc3","decision":"reject","rationale":"The described syntax error is not present in the code under review. cargo check -p tank_core succeeds, egg_dropping() has balanced braces, and causes is still in scope at the event emission call."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-c0817a06","decision":"accept","rationale":"egg_drop_temp_swing_c is defined, defaulted, serialized, mentioned in comments, and asserted in tests, but it is not read by runtime logic. That leaves a dead configuration parameter and stale behavior documentation, so it should either be removed everywhere or wired back into egg-dropping."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-52f42a9a","decision":"reject","rationale":"This issue is already fixed in the current tree. The runtime suppression factor list includes molt_stress, snapshot generation delegates to that shared logic, and the dedicated test test_snapshot_uses_runtime_suppression_labels passes with molt_stress reported as the dominant suppressor."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-3d54a6d2","decision":"accept","rationale":"EventCause::HighDensity is currently dead code. A repository-wide search shows the variant is only defined in the enum and never emitted, so it is either missing instrumentation or unnecessary API surface that should be removed."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-82009a69","decision":"accept","rationale":"The regression is real. egg_dropping() now gates only on the smoothed instability_index, while update_stability_tracker() moves that index only 30% toward a higher raw value per day. From a stable baseline, even a 4°C shock yields about 0.3 instability on day one, below the default 0.5 threshold, so immediate shock-driven egg drops no longer happen."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-98b094a7","decision":"accept","rationale":"This is a concrete failing regression. In the starved scenario, zeroing shrimp_periphyton_grazing_g_per_shrimp_per_day makes shrimp_target_food_route_g() return 0, and update_condition() treats that as fully satiated with food_factor = 1.0. cargo test -p tank_core --test reproduction_factors fails exactly because the starved tank ends up healthier than the fed tank."},{"amendment_id":"fr-5-7f760efe","decision":"accept","rationale":"This failure is also real and currently reproducible. cargo test -p tank_core --test reproduction_factors fails test_mature_stable_tank_breeds_well because the run produces only one ShrimpBerried event while the assertion still requires at least three, so the branch is red until the scenario or expectation is corrected."}]}